        "pkcontributionId": 65341,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vulva</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65342,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Presentation is usually with a painless swelling. There may be pain if there is associated inflammation or ulceration.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65343,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are uncommon vulvar lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65344,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cysts can arise secondary to obstruction of a duct or when epithelium becomes entrapped, for example after surgery or trauma. Cysts of the canal of Nuck are secondary to prolapse of a mesothelial-lined cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65345,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65346,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic features are of a cyst containing fluid that may be watery, mucoid, inspissated, or sebaceous.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65347,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cysts lined by benign mucinous and/or ciliated epithelium occur in the vulvar vestibule. Epidermal inclusion cysts are lined by squamous epithelium, and cysts of the canal of Nuck by benign mesothelium. Cystic endometriosis may also occur {1168323; 7437387; 628540; 14676001; 23496239}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65348,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:29:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
